ewed-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1371324" owner_email="henryhsu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/arc-camera" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/arc-camera" ref="refs/changes/24/1371324/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0bb76344cece38e1076e05ed882303f87ccbfd4a" commit="34ff2125ee8d4568b75b6990aab62e5c33730ed2" commit_message="CRAS: Add a new field to represent when pending streams will start  If one stream is attached to two divices, both iodevs will use the same next_cb_ts. Suppose one is a pending stream and another is a running stream. If audio thread fetchs the running stream first, it will cause next_cb_ts to be changed so that the pending stream will not be moved into running streams list forever.  To fix it, we need to add new field init_cb_ts, which is the time when pending stream should be moved to running stream. And then we don't need to worry that next_cb_ts is changed from other dev_stream which has the same rstream.  BUG=b:121339677 TEST=Audio works fine after changing playback devices.  Change-Id: I0bb76344cece38e1076e05ed882303f87ccbfd4a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1391928 Commit-Ready: Yu-Hsuan Hsu &lt;yuhsuan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yu-Hsuan Hsu &lt;yuhsuan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1391928" owner_email="yuhsuan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/28/1391928/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="11511.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>